  "decision_conditions": [
    "Sufficient evidence has been submitted to demonstrate on a ‘balance of probabilities’ that the use of the rear building at Embassy Lodge, 167 Green Lanes, London, N16 9DH, as two self-contained flats (Flat 19 and Flat 20) (Class C3), has been continuously occupied in excess of 4 years and is, therefore, immune from planning enforcement action as set out in s171b of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\n\nGiven that the burden of proof, on the balance of probability, has been discharged, it is considered that this application for a certificate of lawfulness should now succeed."
